; Activity before a budget's definition. A budget exists from its `budget` directive on, in ledger order: the
; postings and budget-adds before it are not its own, and are reported (a posting once per account and budget). Its
; months start with the month of its definition. An account linked to it before it exists counts from the definition
; on.
option "operating_currency" "CNY"
option "timezone" "UTC"

1970-01-01 commodity CNY

2024-01-01 open Assets:Bank
2024-01-01 open Expenses:Food
  budget: Food
2024-01-01 open Expenses:Snacks
  budget: Food

2024-01-10 * "Market" "January, before the budget"
  Expenses:Food 10 CNY
  Assets:Bank

2024-01-20 * "Kiosk" "January, before the budget, another account"
  Expenses:Snacks 3 CNY
  Assets:Bank

2024-02-01 * "Market" "February, still before the budget"
  Expenses:Food 20 CNY
  Assets:Bank

2024-02-03 budget-add Food 70 CNY

2024-02-15 budget Food CNY
2024-02-15 budget-add Food 500 CNY

2024-02-20 * "Market" "February, after the budget"
  Expenses:Food 30 CNY
  Assets:Bank

2024-03-05 * "Kiosk" "March"
  Expenses:Snacks 4 CNY
  Assets:Bank
